  "domain": "procedural_asset/filter/levels",
  "description": "Filter golden of phase3.2_proc-filter-families (held-out): levels cases on the delivered Skeletal Mage tunic v10 low mesh (one UV tile), texture set 1024 px, L32F User channels. Every User channel is a fill of the authored content-grey bitmap (UV projection, tiled 4 x 4, Nearest, so one bitmap texel per texel); User0 is that content alone, and each case adds one content effect on its own channel, the starter-asset filter found by the documented search s:starterassets u:filter n:<name>= with the case's parameters, or the native levels effect: User1 defaults: the native levels effect (defaults); User2 recipe-bracer-r: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.42, input_max = 0.6, gamma = 1.0, output_min = 0.0, output_max = 1.0, clamp = 0); User3 interior-a: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.1, input_max = 0.85, gamma = 1.7, output_min = 0.05, output_max = 0.9, clamp = 0); User4 interior-b: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.3, input_max = 0.55, gamma = 0.4, output_min = 0.2, output_max = 0.95, clamp = 1). Painter then bakes World Space Normals low as high (OutputSize 10, LowAsHigh, DilationWidth 0, every other baking parameter at Painter's default) to mark its UV coverage. The User maps and the World Space Normals map are exported as OpenEXR 32f, padding passthrough, no dithering; recorded twice (same session; after save and reopen). Bake backend uncontrolled.",
